meta {
  name: Sign In
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{clientUrl}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{ownerEmail}}",
    "password": "{{password}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Run this first. Bruno keeps the session cookie in its cookie jar, and every
  other request in this collection relies on it.

  403 MISSING_OR_NULL_ORIGIN means the Origin header is missing. Better Auth runs
  a CSRF check on any state changing request that carries a cookie, so every
  non-GET request here sends Origin: {{clientUrl}}, which is in trustedOrigins.

  403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED means the account exists but has not verified its email.
}
